{
  "description": "The 909 (909.json) moved toward an 80s drum computer on five pads; its hats, cymbals, rim and percussion are the 909's. The kick: 1.65 semitones up (55 Hz), shorter (78 ms against 100), its sweep quicker, its noise click low-passed at 3.2 kHz instead of 5, driven harder. The snare: 2.2 semitones down, its body tone 7.6 dB louder and longer (55 ms), its low noise band at 1.4 kHz instead of 7 and lasting 125 ms, its high band from 3.8 kHz instead of 2.6. The clap: its four bursts 13 ms apart instead of 9, its tail 110 ms instead of 55. The toms: 1.5 to 3.5 semitones lower, each sweep slower (55 ms against 30) and each decay longer (120 ms). Its knobs are the 909's: `decay` scales every tone's and band's decay (1: as built), `tone` moves the bands' and the high-pass's cutoffs an octave either way and the noise and the click with them (0.5: as built), `tune` shifts every pitch in semitones. An accent (X) is a quarter louder; a closed hat chokes the open one.",
  "options": {
    "decay": [
      {
        "path": "pads/*/amp*/time",
        "op": "mul"
      },
      {
        "path": "pads/*/amp*/time/amount",
        "op": "mul"
      },
      {
        "path": "pads/*/env*/time",
        "op": "mul"
      },
      {
        "path": "pads/*/env*/time/amount",
        "op": "mul"
      }
    ],
    "tone": [
      {
        "path": "pads/*/band*/frequency",
        "op": "octaves",
        "scale": 2,
        "offset": -1
      },
      {
        "path": "pads/*/highpass/frequency",
        "op": "octaves",
        "scale": 2,
        "offset": -1
      },
      {
        "path": "pads/*/noise/gain_db",
        "op": "mul",
        "offset": 0.5
      },
      {
        "path": "pads/*/click/gain_db",
        "op": "mul",
        "offset": 0.5
      }
    ],
    "tune": [
      {
        "path": "pads/*/tone*/tune",
        "op": "add"
      },
      {
        "path": "pads/*/tri*/tune",
        "op": "add"
      },
      {
        "path": "pads/*/metal/tune",
        "op": "add"
      }
    ]
  },
